WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.975
This comparison helps distinguish GROUPING SETS
ROLLUP and CUBE GROUPING SETS returns

00:00:05.988 --> 00:00:11.438
only the combinations you explicitly list If you
request category totals product

00:00:11.462 --> 00:00:17.025
totals and a grand total PostgreSQL returns exactly
those levels ROLLUP of

00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:21.125
A and B follows a hierarchy It produces A and B
together

00:00:21.312 --> 00:00:24.838
then A alone then the empty grouping set which
represents the grand

00:00:24.850 --> 00:00:29.638
total It does not automatically produce B alone
because the hierarchy moves

00:00:29.662 --> 00:00:33.488
from detailed to broader levels from left to right
CUBE of A

00:00:33.512 --> 00:00:37.138
and B returns every combination A and B together A
alone B

00:00:37.162 --> 00:00:41.162
alone and the grand total A useful way to choose
among them

00:00:41.175 --> 00:00:44.900
is to think about the report design If the
dimensions have a

00:00:44.925 --> 00:00:49.788
natural parent-child relationship ROLLUP is often a
good fit If you want

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:54.800
every cross-dimensional subtotal CUBE may be
appropriate If the report needs a

00:00:54.825 --> 00:00:59.812
custom set of levels GROUPING SETS gives you precise
control These features

00:00:59.838 --> 00:01:03.438
can create more rows than beginners expect so always
inspect the grain

00:01:03.450 --> 00:01:06.000
of each result row and label subtotal rows clearly
